# A scratch client for this server's three verbs. Send a request from the gutter in Visual Studio.
#
# This file shipped as the Web SDK template's example and called `get_random_number` on port 5144
# — a tool that never existed on a port this project never used. It is now the shortest way to
# check the surface by hand: the same walk the protocol tests automate.

@HostAddress = http://localhost:6217

### Every tool there is. Expect exactly three: orient, query, commit.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list","params":{}}

### Start here. What this system is, what exists in it, and what to call next.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"orient","arguments":{}}}

### The exact catalog: every kind, the parameters it reads, every payload shape.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"kind":"capabilities"}}}

### The operating manual.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"kind":"procedures"}}}

### One contract in full. Reads are recorded, and a later commit reports what was actually opened.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"kind":"procedures","id":"procedure.system.use"}}}

### What the world holds, and which component definitions exist.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":6,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"kind":"world"}}}

### The rules that exist, searched the way a player would say it.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":7,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"kind":"mechanics","query":"can they manage it"}}}

### Declare a component definition. Note payload is a JSON object encoded as a STRING.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":8,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"commit","arguments":{"kind":"component","payload":"{\"id\":\"stats\",\"name\":\"Stats\",\"description\":\"Numbers about an entity.\"}","intent":"set up a scratch world"}}}

### Change the world. dryRun first, always — then send the identical payload without it.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":9,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"commit","arguments":{"kind":"effects","payload":"{\"effects\":[{\"type\":\"entity.create\",\"entityId\":\"orban\",\"name\":\"Orban\"},{\"type\":\"component.set\",\"entityId\":\"orban\",\"definitionId\":\"stats\",\"data\":\"{\\\"vigour\\\":6}\"}]}","dryRun":true,"intent":"create a character","proceduresUsed":["procedure.world.change"]}}}

### Resolve an action. This RUNS a rule — selection is by intent, and there is no dry run.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":10,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"commit","arguments":{"kind":"action","payload":"{\"intent\":\"can they manage it\",\"roleEntityIds\":{\"subject\":\"orban\"},\"input\":\"{\\\"field\\\":\\\"vigour\\\",\\\"threshold\\\":5}\"}","proceduresUsed":["procedure.action.run"]}}}

### What has been done, newest first. Add failuresOnly or subject to narrow it.
POST {{HostAddress}}/mcp
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":11,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"kind":"history","limit":20}}}
